    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d713">

                <pb facs="0680" n="590" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg590"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/807</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Tiflis</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1917-12-15T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 15,
                                1917, 6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your telegrams December 4, 9 p.m., and subsequent dates including December 13, 6
                    p.m., received. Department appreciates your thorough reports on situation, is in
                    touch with Allied Governments, and hopes to give you definite instructions
                    shortly on whole subject. Meanwhile do not commit this Government. No country
                    either belligerent or neutral has recognized Bolshevik government,
                    Petrograd.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[For a description of the development of the anti-Bolshevik movement of the
                        Cossacks under Kaledin during the first days of December 1917, see despatch
                        No. 212 of December 15, 1917, from the Consul General at Moscow, <ref
                            target="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg_304">Volume I, page 304</ref>.]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
